// Example 03: objects and enums.
//
// Values with parts. An object is a fixed set of named fields; an enum is
// a closed list of alternatives, and an alternative can carry fields of
// its own. Every shape has a name, and two shapes with the same fields
// are still different types.
//
// The project is a bakery's cake orders. README.md lists the files in
// reading order.
